body:
For the purpose of this challenge I wanted to have the `jobid` be short for the end user. Ideally I wanted to use something like `UUIDv7`.

1. Note: Im using the `crypto/rand` package which automatically seeds the rand function.
```go
import (
	"crypto/rand"
	"math/big"
	"strings"
)

const letters = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789"

func randomString(n int) string {
	var sb strings.Builder
	for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
		num, _ := rand.Int(rand.Reader, big.NewInt(int64(len(letters))))
		sb.WriteByte(letters[num.Int64()])
	}
	return sb.String()
}
```
2. I believe 5 bytes of random is too small yes. I could extend this to 10 bytes of random to make it more robust.

