body:
~~As stated above, I can't put a process directly into a `cgroup` unless I use a `SYS_CLONE3` system call which I can't do via `os/exec` at the moment.  If the `cgroup` race condition window wasn't an issue then I could. I researched some and even the go implementations like `containerd`  have this same issue. There is a moment between `fork` and `exec` where the `pid` is being moved into the `cgroup` that is an attack window. The Linux kernel 5.7+  the `clone` syscall now how `CLONE_INTO_CGROUP` as to resolve this issue.  The will remove the window completely but complicates the code and makes it low level.~~

Update: I will use os/exec.Cmd with Go1.21+ . Doc will reflect details

@zmb3

Oh. I think it does actually. Not full clone args support but what we need to do this yes. This will simplify the code quite a bit so its not so low level. 

I will implement this same flow but with Go's higher constructs.
@rosstimothy

